Subject: [PATCH 4/4] refactor(sim): _sim_hawkes_bg cell rates are
 background_masses(...) -- a new likelihood.py atom, the integrand of the
 background compensators -- so simulator and likelihood share ONE
 background-mass expression. Per review: NO runtime cross-check (it would be
 tautological now that both sides derive from the shared atom); enforcement
 lives in unit tests pinning sum(background_masses) against
 constant/covariate_background_integral. Per-cell Poisson superposition
 retained (distributionally identical to Poisson(total) + multinomial);
 locations drawn through the shared, length-guarded _sample_cells primitive;
 _sim_spatial retired (single caller, absorbed). Legacy quirk preserved and
 documented in the docstring: the pure-Hawkes sample_points draw is UNSEEDED
 (ignores np.random and the rng argument) -- RECORDED FOLLOW-UP: thread one
 numpy Generator through Poisson counts, inverse-CDF uniforms, cell choices,
 sample_points, offspring counts, and trigger simulation; until then
 simulate() is not fully seed-reproducible on this path. Verified: 38/38;
 inference value+gradient pins bit-identical.

